(Regression test: a function definition whose body ends in a top-level
Return used to silently swallow the next top-level sentence into the
function body as dead code whenever the author omitted the separating
blank line. LANGUAGE.md states blank lines are optional and have no
effect on program execution, so the call below must run at top level
and produce real output. Before the fix it printed nothing because the
Print statement was emitted after the function's return epilogue.)

To "double" with a number called "x". Return a number, x multiply 2.
Print "double" of 21.
Print "double" of 5.